<!doctype html>
<!--
  Crossbearing — Agent Attribution Audit
  Emitted by `crossbearing report --format html`. The numbers, findings, and
  provenance are the real join output; the chrome is the wedge deliverable.
  Open in a browser → Print → "Save as PDF" (@page is set for Letter).
  Brand: paper #f2efe9 · ink #182433 · sea-blue fix #0b96d6.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Agent Attribution Audit — crossbearing</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --paper: #f2efe9;
        --paper-200: #d8d2c4;
        --ink: #182433;
        --ink-700: #243446;
        --ink-500: #3c5067;
        --ink-400: #5a6f86;
        --fix: #0b96d6;
        --sans: "IBM Plex Sans", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
        --mono: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
        --display: "Fraunces", Georgia, serif;
      }
      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        font-family: var(--sans);
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--paper);
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.55;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      .page { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 40px 64px; }
      .tick { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); }
      .mono { font-family: var(--mono); }
      .rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-200); margin: 18px 0; }
      .sheet {
        background: #fbfaf7;
        border: 1px solid var(--paper-200);
        border-radius: 2px;
        box-shadow: 0 1px 1px rgba(24,36,51,0.04), 0 4px 10px rgba(24,36,51,0.05), 0 12px 24px rgba(24,36,51,0.04);
        padding: 18px 20px;
      }
      .head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
      .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; }
      .brand .name { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); }
      .tag {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fix);
        border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--fix) 30%, transparent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fix) 9%, white); padding: 3px 7px;
      }
      .eyebrow { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fix); margin-top: 28px; }
      .meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 14px; }
      .meta .k { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); }
      .meta .v { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-700); margin-top: 2px; }
      .headline {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 27px; line-height: 1.18; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin: 26px 0 6px; max-width: 30ch;
      }
      .headline em { font-style: italic; color: var(--fix); font-weight: 600; }
      .subhead { color: var(--ink-500); font-size: 14px; max-width: 62ch; }
      .strip {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--paper-200);
        border: 1px solid var(--paper-200); margin: 22px 0 6px;
      }
      .stat { background: #fbfaf7; padding: 14px 14px 12px; }
      .stat .n { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 30px; line-height: 1; color: var(--ink); }
      .stat.flag .n { color: var(--fix); }
      .stat .l { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); margin-top: 8px; }
      .section { margin-top: 34px; }
      .section > h2 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; }
      .section > h2 .idx { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--fix); font-weight: 500; }
      .section > p.lede { color: var(--ink-500); margin-top: 6px; max-width: 70ch; }
      .findings { margin-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
      .finding .op { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
      .finding .op .badge {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: white;
        background: var(--fix); padding: 2px 6px; margin-left: 8px; vertical-align: middle;
      }
      .kv { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 13px; }
      .kv .k { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); padding-top: 2px; }
      .kv .v { color: var(--ink-700); }
      .why { margin-top: 10px; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 2px solid var(--fix); color: var(--ink-700); font-size: 13px; }
      .prov { margin-top: 10px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-400); word-break: break-all; }
      .prov .loc { color: var(--ink-500); }
      .diverge { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0; margin-top: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--paper-200); }
      .diverge > div { padding: 12px 14px; }
      .diverge .claim { border-right: 1px solid var(--paper-200); background: #fbfaf7; }
      .diverge .record { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fix) 6%, #fbfaf7); }
      .diverge .side { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); }
      .diverge .val { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 6px; }
      .next {
        margin-top: 34px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--fix) 35%, var(--paper-200));
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fix) 7%, white); padding: 22px 24px; border-radius: 2px;
      }
      .next h3 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 17px; }
      .next p { color: var(--ink-700); margin-top: 8px; max-width: 64ch; }
      .next .cta {
        display: inline-block; margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        background: var(--fix); color: white; padding: 9px 16px; text-decoration: none;
      }
      .fine { margin-top: 30px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-500); }
      .fine h4 { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-400); margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .fine ul { margin-left: 16px; }
      .fine li { margin: 4px 0; }
      .foot { margin-top: 34px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-200); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
      @page { size: letter; margin: 16mm; }
      @media print {
        body { background: #fff; }
        .page { padding: 0; max-width: none; }
        .sheet, .finding, .next, .strip { break-inside: avoid; }
        .section { break-inside: avoid-page; }
        * { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <header class="head">
        <span class="brand">
          <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 256 256" aria-hidden="true">
            <g fill="none" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-width="12">
              <line x1="61.5" y1="232" x2="149.5" y2="40" stroke="#182433" />
              <line x1="70" y1="38.8" x2="210" y2="203.5" stroke="#182433" />
              <line x1="12" y1="160.6" x2="244" y2="127.4" stroke="#0b96d6" />
            </g>
            <circle cx="126" cy="128.8" r="9" fill="#0b96d6" />
          </svg>
          <span class="name">crossbearing</span>
        </span>
        <span class="tag">read-only · agent attribution audit</span>
      </header>

      <div class="eyebrow">Agent Attribution Audit</div>
      <div class="meta">
        <div>
          <div class="k">Prepared for</div>
          <div class="v">{{with .PreparedFor}}{{.}}{{else}}—{{end}}</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="k">AWS account</div>
          <div class="v mono">{{.Account}}</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="k">Window</div>
          <div class="v">{{.Window}}</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="k">Generated</div>
          <div class="v">{{.Generated}}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="rule" />

      {{if eq .Mode "unattributed"}}
      <h1 class="headline">
        Of {{.Sessions}} agent sessions in this window,
        <em>{{.UnattributedN}} production-touching {{.ActionWord}}</em>
        trace{{.TraceSuffix}} to no named human.
      </h1>
      <p class="subhead">
        Your cloud recorded each one. Nothing in your organization can say which agent run,
        or which person, they belong to. These are the lines an auditor circles.
      </p>
      {{else if eq .Mode "divergent"}}
      <h1 class="headline">
        Every recorded action here <em>traces to a named human</em>. But
        <em>{{.DivergentN}} agent {{.ClaimWord}}</em> diverge{{.DivergeSuffix}} from the record.
      </h1>
      <p class="subhead">
        No production action is orphaned. Where the agent's own account disagrees with what
        your cloud logged is below. A receipt alone would miss that gap.
      </p>
      {{else}}
      <h1 class="headline">
        Every production-touching action in this window <em>traces to a named human.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="subhead">
        Across {{.Sessions}} agent sessions, your cloud's own record binds each action to a
        person, and each claim matches the record. That is the answer an auditor wants. Most
        accounts can't give it.
      </p>
      {{end}}

      <div class="strip" style="grid-template-columns: repeat({{len .Stats}}, 1fr)">
        {{range .Stats}}
        <div class="stat{{if .Flag}} flag{{end}}">
          <div class="n">{{.N}}</div>
          <div class="l">{{.Label}}</div>
        </div>
        {{end}}
      </div>
      {{with .StreamsLine}}<p class="tick" style="margin-top: 10px">{{.}}</p>{{end}}

      {{if .HasAgentSuspect}}
      <section class="section">
        <h2><span class="idx">01a</span> Agent-suspect — fingerprinted to an agent</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          These {{len .UnattributedAgentSuspect}} unattributed actions carry an agent
          fingerprint — a proven credential session or a named role session — so they are the
          ones to look at first. The full unattributed set, including same-principal bystander
          activity, is in 01 below; nothing here is removed from it.
        </p>
        <div class="findings">
          {{range .UnattributedAgentSuspect}}
          <div class="finding sheet">
            <div class="op">{{.Operation}} <span class="badge">agent-suspect</span></div>
            <div class="kv">
              {{range .KVs}}<div class="k">{{.K}}</div><div class="v mono">{{.V}}</div>{{end}}
            </div>
            <div class="why">{{.Reason}}</div>
            <div class="prov"><span class="loc">{{.Locator}}</span> · {{.Digest}} · re-fetchable</div>
          </div>
          {{end}}
        </div>
      </section>
      {{end}}

      {{if .HasUnattributed}}
      <section class="section">
        <h2><span class="idx">01</span> Production-touching actions with no named human</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A production-scoped action your cloud recorded, attributable to an agent
          credential session but to no person. SourceIdentity is opt-in: unless the role's
          trust policy requires it and the caller sets it on AssumeRole, the field is empty
          and nothing binds the action to a human (STS SourceIdentity, a session tag, or
          Kubernetes impersonation).
        </p>
        <div class="findings">
          {{range .Unattributed}}
          <div class="finding sheet">
            <div class="op">{{.Operation}} <span class="badge">{{.Badge}}</span></div>
            <div class="kv">
              {{range .KVs}}<div class="k">{{.K}}</div><div class="v mono">{{.V}}</div>{{end}}
            </div>
            <div class="why">{{.Why}}</div>
            <div class="prov"><span class="loc">{{.Locator}}</span> · {{.Digest}} · re-fetchable</div>
          </div>
          {{end}}
        </div>
      </section>
      {{end}}

      {{if .HasDivergences}}
      <section class="section">
        <h2><span class="idx">{{if .HasUnattributed}}02{{else}}01{{end}}</span> Divergences — claim vs. record</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The agent's own account said one thing; your cloud recorded another, in the same
          window. The claim side is the agent's story. These are where it disagrees with the
          record.
        </p>
        <div class="findings">
          {{range .Divergences}}
          <div class="finding sheet">
            <div class="diverge">
              <div class="claim">
                <div class="side">Agent claimed</div>
                <div class="val">{{.ClaimValue}}</div>
              </div>
              <div class="record">
                <div class="side">Cloud recorded</div>
                <div class="val">{{.RecordValue}}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="kv">
              {{range .KVs}}<div class="k">{{.K}}</div><div class="v">{{.V}}</div>{{end}}
            </div>
            <div class="prov">
              {{if .ClaimLocator}}claim <span class="loc">{{.ClaimLocator}}</span>{{end}}
              {{if .RecordLocator}}⇄ record <span class="loc">{{.RecordLocator}}</span>{{end}}
            </div>
          </div>
          {{end}}
        </div>
      </section>
      {{end}}

      <div class="next">
        <h3>What this is, and what makes it continuous</h3>
        <p>
          This is a snapshot from a single window, produced from read-only access to logs you
          already keep. The <strong>Agent Audit-Readiness engagement</strong> wires the
          attribution conventions so it runs continuously, maps every finding to the controls
          in your next audit (SOC&nbsp;2 CC6.1 / CC7.2 / CC8.1; ISO&nbsp;42001 Annex&nbsp;A
          A.3.2 / A.6.2.8 / A.6.2.6), and seals it into an Agent Evidence Package your auditor
          can verify without us: hash-chained, signed under your own KMS key.
        </p>
        <a class="cta" href="mailto:hello@crossbearing.dev?subject=crossbearing%20attribution%20audit%20%E2%86%92%20engagement">Make it continuous →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="fine">
        <h4>How this was produced</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Read-only.</strong> No proxy, no hook, nothing in the agent path; the
            engine consumes logs you already keep and no data left your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Corroborated.</strong> What each agent claimed (a Claude Code transcript
            or Bedrock invocation log) was joined against your cloud's own record by window
            and operation. The engine reads five record streams out of the box: CloudTrail,
            GitHub audit, Kubernetes audit, GCP Cloud Audit Logs, and Azure Activity Log.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Re-fetchable, not asserted.</strong> Every finding carries a locator +
            SHA-256 digest of the raw event. Your team or your auditor can resolve each one
            independently.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="foot">
        <span class="brand">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 256 256" aria-hidden="true">
            <g fill="none" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-width="14">
              <line x1="61.5" y1="232" x2="149.5" y2="40" stroke="#182433" />
              <line x1="70" y1="38.8" x2="210" y2="203.5" stroke="#182433" />
              <line x1="12" y1="160.6" x2="244" y2="127.4" stroke="#0b96d6" />
            </g>
            <circle cx="126" cy="128.8" r="10" fill="#0b96d6" />
          </svg>
          <span class="tick">crossbearing · agent evidence</span>
        </span>
        <span class="tick">read-only · in your account · independently verifiable</span>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
